##-- Idle configuration ------------------
##
## Sway's idle daemon (swayidle) runs the given commands after the given
## timeouts. All timeouts are in seconds.
##
## Current behavior:
##   5 minutes  : lock the screen
##  10 minutes  : turn off the display (dpms off)
##  on resume   : turn the display back on
##  before sleep: lock the screen
##
## The lockscreen command is a script (see scripts/lockscreen). This is
## deliberate: it lets the theme system swap the lock screen appearance
## without touching this file.

exec swayidle -w \
    timeout  300 "$lockscreen" \
    timeout  600 'swaymsg "output * dpms off"' \
    resume        'swaymsg "output * dpms on"' \
    before-sleep  "$lockscreen"

